# Local model consequences for the full 13.5.21 catalogue

The natural binary linear rows are excluded on the original chief sections
using their action equivalences and the source moved plane. The L₃(2) branch
is excluded using the original nontrivial two-residual image. Further row-wise
group exclusions and surviving-model identifications remain separate source
obligations; this interface does not replace the full B.4.2/B.4.5 boundary.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, 13.5.21,
printed p.924 (PDF p.941).
-/
